# Canopy-destination secrets overlay [OPS.37 / INF.16]. Kamal (2.12) reads
# `secrets-common` + `secrets.<destination>` for a `-d canopy` run, and the
# destination file WINS on key collision — that is the whole mechanism here.
#
# WHY this file exists: Redis isolation for canopy lived ONLY in the CI job
# (deploy.yml maps secrets.CANOPY_REDIS_URL into $REDIS_URL), so a LOCAL
# `kamal deploy -d canopy` — the very command DEPLOY-DAY Phase 3 names — would
# read secrets-common's REDIS_URL=$REDIS_URL from the operator's shell and put
# staging on the PRODUCTION Redis. This overlay makes both legs read the same
# canopy value structurally.
#
# ⚠️ Fallback is a LOUD placeholder on purpose, never $REDIS_URL: a silent
# fall-through to the production URL is exactly the defect this file removes.
# With CANOPY_REDIS_URL unset the container gets an invalid URL → Redis client
# fails loudly and /ready 503s, instead of quietly sharing production state.
# Local run:  export CANOPY_REDIS_URL=rediss://… ; kamal deploy -d canopy
#
# 🔴 THE FORM IS `$(printf '%s' "\${TWIN:-MARKER}")`, NOT `${TWIN:-MARKER}` — and the
# difference was measured on the first canopy boot (2026-09-02): Kamal parses this file
# with Dotenv, whose variable regex accepts `${NAME` and stops at the `:`, so the bash
# default syntax came out as `<value>:-CANOPY_REDIS_URL_NOT_SET}` — a corrupted URL
# WHEN SET (Puma's before_fork raised URI::InvalidURIError on the real Upstash URL) and
# `:-MARKER}` when unset. The `$( … )` form hands the expression to a real shell
# (Kamal's InlineCommandSubstitution runs it via backticks) and the `\$` keeps Dotenv's
# variable pass off it, so `${TWIN:-MARKER}` is evaluated by /bin/sh exactly as written.
# Verified through `Kamal::Secrets` itself for set and unset, and pinned by
# spec/deploy/kamal_secrets_parse_spec.rb — a gate that READS this file as text cannot
# tell the two forms apart; only the parser can (`ssot-maintenance` guard-craft #117).
REDIS_URL=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_REDIS_URL:-CANOPY_REDIS_URL_NOT_SET}")

# [INF.27 move (2), 2026-09-02] TESTNET RPC remaps — same shape as REDIS_URL above, and the
# same reason: the base names resolve to the PRODUCTION (mainnet) secrets in secrets-common,
# so a destination run without these four lines would hand staging mainnet endpoints. The
# boot guard would refuse that (`WEB3_CHAIN_ENV: testnet` in config/deploy.canopy.yml), but a
# refusal is a DETECTOR, not an isolation — this overlay is the isolation, and the refusal is
# what stands behind it. Fallback is a LOUD placeholder on purpose: an unset CANOPY_* twin
# gives the guard a non-testnet "URL" (no chain marker) and it refuses, never a silent
# mainnet call. All four are judged by `scripts/deploy_secret_scan.rb` invariant B4.
# Local run:  export CANOPY_ALCHEMY_POLYGON_RPC_URL=… (and the other three) ; kamal deploy -d canopy
ALCHEMY_POLYGON_RPC_URL=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ALCHEMY_POLYGON_RPC_URL:-CANOPY_ALCHEMY_POLYGON_RPC_URL_NOT_SET}")
ALCHEMY_ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ALCHEMY_ETHEREUM_RPC_URL:-CANOPY_ALCHEMY_ETHEREUM_RPC_URL_NOT_SET}")
SOLANA_RPC_URL=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_SOLANA_RPC_URL:-CANOPY_SOLANA_RPC_URL_NOT_SET}")
CELO_RPC_URL=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_CELO_RPC_URL:-CANOPY_CELO_RPC_URL_NOT_SET}")

# [OPS.37 ⚖️ founder 2026-09-02] TESTNET SIGNER remaps — same shape, same reason, and the
# sharpest instance of it: the base names in secrets-common resolve to the PRODUCTION money
# quintet (Environment `production`, unreadable from the canopy workflow → present-empty ""),
# so canopy's `job:` role WITHOUT these lines would boot on "" and be refused by
# Web3NetworkGuard — or, on a local run with production keys in the operator's shell, SIGN
# REAL VALUE FROM STAGING. The overlay is the isolation; the guard is the detector behind it.
# The twins are throwaway testnet EOAs (the Amoy/Sepolia oracles that hold the roles granted
# by the 2026-09-01/02 deploys · a Celo-Sepolia signer · the Devnet fee-payer) — repo-level
# `CANOPY_*` secrets, never Environment `production`. Judged by `deploy_secret_scan` B4; the
# unset form is a placeholder the guard's key-FORMAT check refuses at boot (not 64 hex).
ORACLE_MINTER_PRIVATE_KEY=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ORACLE_MINTER_PRIVATE_KEY:-CANOPY_ORACLE_MINTER_PRIVATE_KEY_NOT_SET}")
ORACLE_SLASHER_PRIVATE_KEY=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ORACLE_SLASHER_PRIVATE_KEY:-CANOPY_ORACLE_SLASHER_PRIVATE_KEY_NOT_SET}")
ORACLE_CELO_PRIVATE_KEY=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ORACLE_CELO_PRIVATE_KEY:-CANOPY_ORACLE_CELO_PRIVATE_KEY_NOT_SET}")
ETHEREUM_ANCHOR_PRIVATE_KEY=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_ETHEREUM_ANCHOR_PRIVATE_KEY:-CANOPY_ETHEREUM_ANCHOR_PRIVATE_KEY_NOT_SET}")
SOLANA_WALLET_KEYPAIR=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_SOLANA_WALLET_KEYPAIR:-CANOPY_SOLANA_WALLET_KEYPAIR_NOT_SET}")
# Solana PUBLIC identifiers of that Devnet fee-payer — global env.secret names, so they ride
# the same overlay; unset → loud marker, which `Solana::MintingService` rejects at first use.
SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_PUBKEY=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_PUBKEY:-CANOPY_SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_PUBKEY_NOT_SET}")
SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT:-CANOPY_SOLANA_FEE_PAYER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_NOT_SET}")
SOLANA_USDC_MINT_ADDRESS=$(printf '%s' "\${CANOPY_SOLANA_USDC_MINT_ADDRESS:-CANOPY_SOLANA_USDC_MINT_ADDRESS_NOT_SET}")
